class.description:
The Steam singleton dynamically loads the Steam API library at runtime. If the library is not found, all methods fail gracefully without crashing. Use [method request_web_api_ticket] to obtain a ticket for [code]ISteamUserAuth/AuthenticateUserTicket[/code], then [method authenticate_with_server] to exchange it for a JWT from your backend. [b]Steam Workshop:[/b] subscribe to, query, download and publish Workshop items (user-generated content). Requests are asynchronous; results arrive through the [code]workshop_*[/code] signals while callbacks are polled every frame. [codeblock] func _ready(): Steam.initialize(480) Steam.workshop_item_installed.connect(_on_item_installed) # Load content the user is already subscribed to. for id in Steam.get_subscribed_items(): if Steam.get_item_state(id) & Steam.WORKSHOP_ITEM_STATE_INSTALLED: load_mod(Steam.get_item_install_info(id)["folder"]) else: Steam.download_item(id)
func _on_item_installed(published_file_id): load_mod(Steam.get_item_install_info(published_file_id)["folder"])
# Publishing: create an item, then upload its content. func publish(folder): Steam.create_workshop_item() var args = await Steam.workshop_item_created # [published_file_id, result, needs_to_accept_agreement] if args[1] != 1: return var handle = Steam.start_item_update(args[0]) Steam.set_item_title(handle, "My Level") Steam.set_item_content(handle, folder) Steam.set_item_preview(handle, "user://preview.png") Steam.set_item_visibility(handle, Steam.WORKSHOP_VISIBILITY_PUBLIC) Steam.submit_item_update(handle, "Initial release") [/codeblock]
